WEBVTT

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.530
Too slow.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.290
Amateur.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.690
I'm no amateur.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.150
You ruined the mood.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.990
You've had enough time to play.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:58.990
Let's go.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.200
<i>Shit, I can't swim...</i>

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.600
Whoa, I caught a big one.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.990
You...

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.940
Was that you I saw glinting over here?

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.770
What are you doing here?

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.020
I'd like to ask you that.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.190
What are you up to?

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.560
Shut up.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.650
I'll never tell you.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.940
Suit yourself. I'll just take this back...

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.110
Hey, don't tell me you've drowned—

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.400
That dumb face of yours is getting damn cocky!

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.340
That was uncalled for! I just saved your life!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.330
What's your deal?!

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.500
<b>#11  Brawl</b>

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.710
I see.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.810
You were forced to endure cruel treatment 
in an assassin training facility,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.120
and in the end, you killed your 
roommate and best friend.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.200
Yeah.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.450
But it turns out he's still alive.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.400
What do you think of that?

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.370
Think about what?

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.580
That Feilang is still alive.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.830
Think? Well, I'm surprised.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.550
Maybe you're glad he's alive.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.640
If I hired you to kill him, could you do it?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.800
Well...

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.520
Fine. I'll ask somebody else.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.720
Putting that aside...

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.460
The "best friend" you supposedly killed has 
shown up right under your nose in Hakata.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.490
I doubt it's a coincidence.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.260
This is the Kakyu 
Association's headquarters.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.400
As you can see, you're in a cell.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.490
Sure looks hopeless, doesn't it?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.220
But I'll give you one chance to get out.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.260
A fight to the death.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.630
The winner goes free.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.720
That's insane!

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.470
We can't do that!

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.830
Of course you can. Your lives depend on it.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.440
Think about it.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:58.550
Is the other guy's life 
more important than yours?

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.240
How come you're soaking wet?

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.190
I saw someone drowning 
and jumped in to save him.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.210
But you can't swim, Sarucchi!

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.160
You had to hold a kickboard in swim class—

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:14.840
Shut up!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.620
Th-That was mean, Sarucchi.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:23.370
The Kakyu Association is getting bold.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.210
They did this even with you around.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.010
They were all dead when I got here.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.290
All of them?

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.350
There should have been two more guys here.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.980
L-Lau-san...

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.020
What happened? Where were you?

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:45.610
The Kakyu Association abducted us.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.220
Did you escape?

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.270
Where's the other?

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.370
Don't tell me...

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.460
I'm sorry. I had to...

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.440
That red-headed bastard.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:01.670
Is he playing with us?

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.310
Hey, you. Tell us where they are.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.770
I'm gonna go kill—

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:06.360
Wait!

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.260
Don't attack the Kakyu Association.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.310
You're changing the plan!

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.520
The situation has changed.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.230
Do not attack them.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.690
I killed a Sheung Wan executive 
in Beijing a little while ago.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:28.230
A large organization with a lot of 
influence based in Shanghai hired me.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.160
That's where I stole the ring.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.490
The hitman who killed their executive 
is now working for the Kakyu Association.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.120
Do you know what Sheung Wan will make of that?

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.590
They'll think that large 
organization is our ally.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.760
Exactly.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.350
They'll be terrified that we have 
backup that doesn't exist.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.930
Lee-san, has something happened?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:57.520
Sheung Wan has proposed a ceasefire.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.440
A ceasefire? All right.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.220
Tonight? Understood.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.360
I will make arrangements.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.530
See? It worked.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.850
Now it's your turn to help me.

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.490
Tell me what to do.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.320
I want personal information...

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:19.960
on about 100,000 people 
who live in this city.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.380
I'd really like to take a shower.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.970
You killed Unoyama, didn't you?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.110
And you killed that executive, Kim.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.360
I was hired to do it.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.650
Who hired you?

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:38.870
Can't say.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.180
Okay, that's fine.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:44.560
It sounds like our interests are aligned.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.580
Who's the redhead?

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.860
Well, I couldn't say.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.820
Probably just some new hitman 
for the Kakyu Association.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:57.240
He was really strong.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:02.290
It feels like things are 
getting dangerous again...

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.520
Hm?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.710
Where'd Lin-chan go?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:13.630
Thanks for 
everything

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.810
Banba-san? What's up?

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:21.380
Lin-kun?

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.370
I haven't seen him today.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.220
Sure thing.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.400
Bye.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.110
He said if I saw you, to tell you

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.780
that he doesn't understand what 
your note meant, so give him a call.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.580
He really is a moron.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.330
Sheung Wan will not encroach on any 
part of the Kakyu Association's territory.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.720
In return, the Kakyu Association will not 
prevent you from entering other areas.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.800
Do we have an agreement?

00:08:56.210 --> 00:09:00.210
Yes. The deal is struck.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:03.180
There is one more condition.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:08.970
Please give us the Submarine Ninja,
who is in your employ.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:13.030
In return, we will hand over 
the hitman we have hired.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.490
You want to avenge your 
comrades, do you not?

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.450
Very well.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.620
P-Please don't!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.190
You must be dreaming.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.010
<b>Hayashi</b>

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.270
Hey, if it isn't Lin-kun!

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.050
Dr. Saeki.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.590
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.950
Need something from the mushroom?

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.310
No, not exactly...

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.410
Oh, right. This is for you.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:06.650
It's a skin care lotion 
we promote at our clinic.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:10.730
It's the perfect size for 
when you're out and about.

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:11.790
Sure, I guess.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.250
Please give it a try.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:15.880
See you.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.720
Yeah, thanks...

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.430
Hey, Lin!

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:23.890
Yamato?

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.560
Good to see you!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.210
I've got some coupons you can have.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:31.080
They were in a wallet I stole.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.290
50% off!

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.580
Not a bad deal, right?

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:35.980
I don't want those.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.610
Just take them.

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.820
Money is valuable.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:40.790
Later.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.330
What's going on?

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.620
Yo, Lin.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.830
Why the hell are you guys here, too?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.060
Nice to see you, too.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.420
Such a meanie.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.640
Surfing the web?

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:00.260
I'll show you some dirty sites.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.680
No. I'm not gay like you.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.590
Now, you two.

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:07.640
Misa-chan can hear you.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.010
Here. This is for you.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.890
Huh? What's this?

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.960
Hakata Torimon buns.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:17.000
I bought them to get revenge on someone, 
but I didn't end up using them.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.030
You can have them. They're really good.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.690
See you.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.910
Running away is for brats.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.490
Hey, mushroom!

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:33.410
I said not to tell anyone I was here!

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.990
You said not to tell Banba-san.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.840
You didn't say anything about anyone else.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.690
Everyone sure is worried about you, Lin-kun!

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.020
They're just teasing me!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.600
Well, if it isn't Lin-san!

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:51.370
What are you gonna give me? Huh?

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.810
Is this e-extortion?!

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:57.690
Oh, I forgot to tell Saito-kun.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.360
<b>Banba Zenji</b>

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:07.730
See? Someone else is worried about you.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:08.730
You gonna answer that?

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.860
Hello, Shigematsu-san. What is it?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.300
Yeah, Lin-kun's right here.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.010
Okay, hold on.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:27.840
<i>Lin, can I run something by you?</i>

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:28.760
What is it?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:35.400
Last night, two men named Hayashi Noriaki 
were murdered in separate incidents.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.120
<i>So?</i>

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:42.320
They both wrote their names 
the same way you do.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.320
<b>Victim: </b>Hayashi Noriaki 
<b>Address:</b> 1-12-26 Chuo Ward, 
Fukuoka City 
<b>Sex:</b> Male 
<b>Age:</b> 73
<b>Employment:</b> Unemployed

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.320
<b>Victim: </b>Hayashi Noriaki
 <b>Address:</b> 8-23-25-205 Sawara Ward, 
Fukuoka City 
<b>Sex:</b> Male 
<b>Age:</b> 30
<b>Employment:</b> Company Employee

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:48.290
<i>A 73-year-old in Fukuoka City's Chuo Ward 
and a 30-year-old in Sawara Ward.</i>

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:51.050
<i>They have nothing in common 
other than their name,</i>

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.790
<i>but I suspect it's the same killer.</i>

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:57.690
<i>They were both cut apart with a large 
knife, and their left eyes were crushed.</i>

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.130
<i>Do you have any idea what it might mean?</i>

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.010
No, I don't.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.920
<i>Okay, then.</i>

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.250
<i>Sorry to have bothered you, Enokida.</i>

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.780
No problem.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.890
Talk to you later.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.100
That guy from the video?

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:17.450
Yeah.

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.060
It was Feilang.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:23.570
I slashed his left eye six years ago.

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:27.510
There's no doubt. The two murders 
were a message meant for me.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.780
He's come for revenge.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.290
What are you gonna do, Lin-kun?

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.890
I'm going to go see him.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:41.750
Mushroom, I need to know which 
Hayashi Noriaki he'll go after next.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.930
Can you help me?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:46.170
Do you think there's anything I can't do?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.790
Leave it to me.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.390
Lin-chan

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.390
Lin-chan 
Lin-chan 
Lin-chan 
Shigematsu-san 
Enokida-kun

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:59.850
What's happened to Lin-chan?

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.370
<i>I'm glad you could make it.</i>

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:04.980
<i>Please, sit.</i>

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:08.970
You've done some impressive work.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.410
I think we can have a long 
and productive relationship.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.880
A toast.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.870
Sure.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.690
To our coming together.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:26.510
I can smell it.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.550
Don't bother.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:34.510
Lee-san!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:35.720
Bastard!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.160
What the hell are you doing?

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:42.260
Something far kinder than 
trying to poison someone.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:45.980
This virus has a cure.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.570
Virus?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:54.260
It's a lethal virus Sheung Wan developed.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.660
I grabbed a vial for myself.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.590
It stays dormant for a week.

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:02.900
After that, it's certain death.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.080
Where's the cure?

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.970
Don't panic. I have it.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.680
If you want to save him, 
you'll do everything I say.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:15.630
Damn, what a thing to do.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.080
<i>So tell me, why the poison?</i>

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.640
<i>I don't see why you'd have anything against me.</i>

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.350
We made a deal with the Sheung Wan executive.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:27.220
A deal to trade hitmen.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:29.900
If it meant giving you to our enemy...

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.640
I see.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:35.910
But the other side may be 
thinking the same thing.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:38.830
Damn it! I wanna kill someone!

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.400
Now, now, Sarucchi.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.790
Don't get bent out of shape.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.360
There's nothing we can do.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:48.930
Sheung Wan is giving up on Hakata.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.380
I know we're on the losing side this time, but...

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.570
I'm talking about that redhead!

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:57.350
I won't feel better until I've killed him!

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.780
Yes, yes.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.410
Eat up.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:02.580
It's on me today.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.610
Hello, this is Nitta.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:16.490
Yes, he's asleep, as per our plan.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.080
I'll see you soon.

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.290
Found it.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.180
This is what the two Hayashi 
Noriakis had in common.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:24.870
What?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.340
They both bought health supplements 
from the same online store.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.470
I've bought that before.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:37.570
It didn't do much, and I started 
getting unsolicited sales calls.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.260
So they're selling off their 
customers' contact info.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:46.410
And the Kakyu Association bought the list.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:48.360
That's how Feilang got their names.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.370
Yeah, which means...

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.320
Bingo.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:58.030
There's one more Hayashi Noriaki 
living in Fukuoka City.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.590
His address is...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.710
<b>Banba Zenji</b>

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.530
Mushroom, send that address to my phone.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:16.530
I owe you one.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.170
Good morning, Sarucchi.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:27.730
You were asleep for quite a while.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:31.150
Hey, what's going on?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:35.660
We have to give you to 
the Kakyu Association.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:39.320
Lau-san asked us to give 
you a sleeping drug.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.260
What did you say?

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.610
We're giving you—

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.010
Nao, you sold me out?!

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:47.170
I'll kill you!

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.670
My, how scary.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.400
Unfortunately, it's you 
who's going to be killed.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.380
Wait a moment. Aren't we 
handing him over alive?

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.960
There's a risk he'll switch sides 
and become a danger to us.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.940
Because you resisted, 
we've decided to kill you.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.060
This is not what we agreed.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:11.650
You can have that money as compensation.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:17.110
You said yourself that hitmen 
are nothing but tools.

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.320
Indeed.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.290
As you say, he's nothing but a tool.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.540
I'm happy to accept this payment.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:28.670
You bastard!

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:33.390
That's the way it is. Sorry, Sarucchi.

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:37.170
You think "sorry" is gonna 
cut it, you piece of shit?!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.420
Lau-san!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.890
Bastard!

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.270
I'm glad I hit him.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:55.530
Recoil hurts more than I expected.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.100
Okay, they're off—

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:03.530
That's mean, Sarucchi!

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.240
You bastard! You betrayed me!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.760
I said I was sorry!

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.920
And I didn't betray you.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.460
I saved you.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.070
You let your emotions get the better of you.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:18.420
You said hitmen were nothing but tools.

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:21.940
I take care of my tools.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:25.930
Especially the ones that are one-of-a-kind.

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.730
Who are you calling a tool?

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.650
And now for the traitor...

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.100
Like I said, I didn't betray you.

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:42.020
I was planning to take Lau's 
money and run from the start.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.240
But he would've caught on if I'd told you.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.960
You're a terrible actor, Sarucchi.

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:51.620
I want 20% of your share.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.500
That sounds a bit low. I'd understand 30%—

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.500
0.152!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.040
That's even lower.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.920
You make it sound like a 
weak batting average—

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:06.360
The next one might actually hit.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.190
<b>Hayashi Noriaki</b>

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:34.330
Hey, Mao, check out the 
fancy watch he's got.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:37.920
Why are you alive?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.920
Because you messed up.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:48.200
The guy who bought the bodies
realized I was alive.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:54.190
He treated my wounds and sold me 
to an old sicko who liked torturing kids.

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.570
Thanks to you, I know 
what Hell is really like.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.360
If only you'd finished me off.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:04.820
So you're here for revenge?

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:08.320
No, I'm here to take you back.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.570
Let's work together, Mao.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:15.250
We'll tour the world, 
making a fortune killing people.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:18.150
We'd make a great team.

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.460
Just like I promised.

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.300
No.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.650
Why not?

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:29.260
Because I betrayed you?

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.040
No, that's not why.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.590
We'll be rich beyond our wildest dreams.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:36.590
After how poor we were as kids.

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.490
I don't care about money.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.470
Why, then?

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:41.940
Why won't you work with me?

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:47.060
I don't want to leave this city.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.030
I like this city!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:53.450
And the people I've met here!

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:56.260
I see.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:58.290
In that case...

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.680
I'll destroy them.

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:05.060
This city... and all your friends!

00:23:03.850 --> 00:23:05.820
Hey, the next episode's the last one.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.970
Is it that fan favorite where 
I get scouted by the Hawks?

00:23:08.970 --> 00:23:09.980
Quit lying!

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.870
New series: <i>Hakata Enokida Hackers</i>.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:12.890
That's not a series!

00:23:12.890 --> 00:23:13.660
You shut up!

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:14.460
What's going on?

00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:14.990
What's up?

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:15.900
You're on my team now.

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.410
Where are you going?

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:17.980
Shut up, all of you!

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:20.460
Hey, everyone! We'll be waiting in Hakata!

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
#12  Walk-Off Home Run
